---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactCTA from '@components/ContactCTA.astro';
const steps = [
  { title: 'Frame the question', body: 'Establish the business context, intended audience, constraints, and the decision the project must support.' },
  { title: 'Investigate', body: 'Examine the existing brand, product, experience, and available evidence. Research methods depend on the brief.' },
  { title: 'Set direction', body: 'Agree on priorities and principles before selecting a visual or product direction.' },
  { title: 'Develop the system', body: 'Create and refine the identity, product, digital experience, or combination required by the work.' },
  { title: 'Support implementation', body: 'Prepare useful specifications and stay close to how the work is made or shipped.' },
  { title: 'Review what happened', body: 'Evaluate the result against the goals and evidence agreed at the start.' },
  { title: 'Evolve deliberately', body: 'Maintain and extend the system when the business, product, or audience changes.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Approach" description="How HS108 frames decisions, develops design systems, supports implementation, and reviews the result.">
  <header class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h1 class="display">A clear path from question to system.</h1><p class="lead">The work begins with the decision a business needs to make. Research, design, implementation, and evaluation follow that question.</p></header>
  <section class="section dark" aria-labelledby="approach-steps-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">The working sequence</p><div><h2 class="section-title" id="approach-steps-title">Seven connected decisions.</h2><p>The depth and pace of each step are agreed for the engagement. This sequence describes the logic, not a fixed package or timeline.</p></div></div><div class="row-list">{steps.map((step,i) => <div class="row-item"><span class="row-num">0{i+1}</span><h3 class="row-title">{step.title}</h3><p class="row-desc">{step.body}</p><span></span></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section shell" aria-labelledby="working-together-title"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Working together</p><div><h2 class="section-title" id="working-together-title">The brief shapes the scope.</h2><p>A first conversation should clarify the problem, the people involved, the constraints, and what a useful next decision looks like. From there, HS108 can recommend a focused project, a discovery engagement, or ongoing support.</p><div class="section-foot"><a class="text-link" href="/programs">Explore engagement models ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
  <ContactCTA />
</BaseLayout>
